graph TB
    subgraph "Standard I/O FILE*"
        A1[fopen/fread/fwrite/fclose]
        A2[User Space Buffering]
        A3[Format Conversion fprintf/fscanf]
        A4[Portable across systems]
    end
    
    subgraph "System Calls - File Descriptors"
        B1[open/read/write/close]
        B2[No buffering direct to kernel]
        B3[Raw binary data]
        B4[Full control maximum performance]
    end
    
    A1 -.->|Uses internally| B1
    A2 -.->|Reduces syscalls| B1
    
    C[When to use?]
    C --> C1[Use FILE* for text formats]
    C --> C2[Use fd for binary, sockets, devices]
    C --> C3[Use fd for low-latency I/O]
    C --> C4[Use FILE* for convenience]
    
    style A2 fill:#e8f5e8
    style B2 fill:#e1f5ff
